+description: Working checklist for writing or changing code so it is correct, handles edge cases, and is verified by tests before being called done. Use when implementing a feature, fixing a bug, refactoring, or otherwise editing source code, especially when the change touches input handling, data transformations, error paths, or behavior other code depends on. Skip it for questions about code that involve no changes.
